{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RYNDVpBNf3pR3PAqCnmgGC","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"success\\\": true, \\\"data\\\": {\\\"path\\\": \\\"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_3/projects/structfuse-context/memory.md\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"# Memory — structfuse-context\\\\n\\\\n## GPU 越界教训 (2026-05-13)\\\\n\\\\n第三次 GPU 越界事件：PID 897752 占用 cuda:0（属于 rl-active-probe-fl），导致对方数据丢失。根因：旧进程或直接运行库模块时未设 CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES，torch 默认使用 cuda:0。\\\\n\\\\n**硬规则**：\\\\n- 项目只有 cuda:5@cqa1-21977，所有 .py 文件（含库模块）必须在 import torch 前用 `os.environ.setdefault(\\\\\\\"CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"5\\\\\\\")` 防护\\\\n- 入口脚本用 `os.environ[\\\\\\\"CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES\\\\\\\"] = \\\\\\\"5\\\\\\\"`（强制覆盖），库模块用 `setdefault`（不覆盖入口已设的值）\\\\n- Worker 提交实验必须用 submit_training_job（自动管理 CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES），禁止 nohup\\\\n\\\\n## ACDC isinf 退化——核心方法论问题 (2026-05-13)\\\\n\\\\nACDC binarization 用 `isinf` 只选出极少边（IOI 14, Arithmetic 17），但 ACDC 实际有 0.03-0.09 四级中间分数。isinf 导致 CSS=1.0 与 ACDC 完全重合，跨方法共识退化。top-k binarization（k=50-75）解决此问题：Arithmetic CSS 3/3 从 17→44-54。\\\\n\\\\n**但 top-k 未翻转条件④**：CSS=1.0 mean CPR=0.919 < EAP-IG=0.985。\\\\n\\\\n## D021: CSS-only 叙事 (2026-05-13)\\\\n\\\\n放弃 CIRCUS 作为独立 claim。转 CSS-only 叙事。\\\\n\\\\n## 竞争定位：CSS vs CIRCUS (2026-05-13)\\\\n\\\\n- **CIRCUS (Parekh, 2026)** 最大竞争对手。CSS 差异化 = method diversity > threshold diversity\\\\n- **Mondorf et al.** direct competitor：仅 gradient 族、score averaging（非 binary consensus）\\\\n- 关键支撑：Miller et al. (COLM 2024) faithfulness 对消融敏感；Méloux et al. EAP/EAP-IG 高方差\\\\n\\\\n## D026: MVP Gate 最终结论 (2026-05-13)\\\\n\\\\n**Arithmetic 条件④ FAIL（CSS=1.0 < EAP-IG），IOI PASS。**\\\\n\\\\n关键教训：\\\\n1. **Zero ablation 是 artifact 源**——所有小电路 zero CPR 为负，mean ablation 翻正到 0.9+\\\\n2. **节点级 ablation 的局限**——CSS=1.0 CPR 在 k=50→75 不变（节点集相同，边数变化无法区分）\\\\n3. **EAP-IG×EP 在 arithmetic 上 Jaccard=0.695**——两方法高度一致，CSS 缺少第三方视角的信息增益\\\\n4. **IOI 上 CSS 边效率极高**——14 edges CPR≈50 edges 单方法，每条边贡献远超单方法\\\\n5. **IOI CPR 不一致是误报**——mean_ablation_results.json 中标注为 IOI 的数据实际是 Arithmetic\\\\n\\\\n**等待 Director 决策：edge-efficiency claim / 原 claim + 更多任务 / pivot。**\\\\n\\\\n## IFR 作为第三方法——已证伪 (2026-05-13)\\\\n\\\\n**phase2_qwen05b_ioi_k3 (negative)**: Qwen-2.5 0.5B 上 IFR 与 EAP-IG/EP 的 Jaccard = 0.00。\\\\n\\\\n**D028 诊断结论**:\\\\n1. **Per-head 分解无效**: IFR 已经在用 per-head 分解，不是修复方向\\\\n2. **根本原因**: IFR (proximity) 度量 activation magnitude → 偏向高幅度 MLP 输出 (m2, m20, m22)；gradient 方法度量 causal influence → 偏向任务关键 attention heads (a20.h9)。两者解构的是不同维度\\\\n3. **Jaccard sweep**: 首次非零在 N=500 (J=0.045)，unique_score_rank 展开到 2191 边也仅 J=0.065\\\\n4. **Destination-side 退化 100%**: 同层头共享 residual stream，所有头得到相同 destination score\\\\n\\\\n**结论**: IFR 不能作为 CSS 第三方法用于大模型。gradient 族内部仍有共识（EAP-IG×EP Jaccard=0.54）。Phase 2 需要替代第三方法（ACDC top-k 或另一个 gradient 方法）。\\\\n\\\", \\\"total_chars\\\": 2263, \\\"truncated\\\": false}, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"metadata\\\": {}}\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01EyvyTJLeHCS14HM3aHx2sg","session_id":"d5948ce3-0bd6-4774-9a29-31d903f57111","uuid":"bb43bfea-6824-45d9-bd8b-c121ca213fa5","timestamp":"2026-05-13T09:56:16.856Z"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01A41hBQ2pF8CCrubDLeErhV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VEc7qrgHBiC2ohLyKcEz7X","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"R2: Novelty + Related Work review","prompt":"You are Reviewer 2 (R2) for a blind peer review. Your focus is **Novelty and Related Work**.\n\n## Venue & Scoring Rubric (EMNLP 2026 via ARR)\n\nUse these scales (0.5 increments):\n- **Soundness** (1-5): 5=Exceptional, 4=Strong (sufficient support for all claims), 3=Acceptable (sufficient for main claims), 2=Poor (main claims not sufficiently supported), 1=Major issues\n- **Excitement** (1-5): 5=Highly exciting, 4=Exciting, 3=Interesting, 2=Potentially interesting, 1=Not exciting\n- **Overall** (1-5): 5=Award, 4=Conference, 3.5=Borderline Conference, 3=Findings, 2.5=Borderline Findings, 2=Resubmit next cycle, 1.5=Resubmit after next cycle\n- **Reproducibility** (1-5): 5=Easily reproducible, 4=Mostly reproducible, 3=Some difficulty, 2=Difficult, 1=Cannot reproduce\n- **Confidence** (1-5): 5=Positive my evaluation is correct, 4=Quite sure, 3=Pretty sure, 2=Willing to defend but may have missed details, 1=Not my area\n\n## Paper Summary\n\n**Title:** \"When Does Circuit Consensus Fail? A Systematic Analysis of Cross-Method Agreement in Mechanistic Interpretability\"\n\nThe paper formalizes a \"Circuit Selection Score\" (CSS) — the fraction of K=3 circuit discovery methods (EAP-IG, EP, ACDC) selecting each edge — and tests whether high-consensus edges (CSS=1.0) outperform individual methods. Evaluated across 4 tasks × 2 models = 6 configurations. Central finding: consensus succeeds in only 1/6 cases (IOI on GPT-2).\n\nThree failure modes:\n1. Task-induced method correlation (bottleneck tasks force convergence → high Jaccard → consensus just selects obvious edges)\n2. Component-level scoring degeneration (Qwen-0.5B: IFR→layer-level due to GQA KV sharing; ACDC→node-level due to 179K edge search space)\n3. Jaccard-predictable failure (max pairwise Jaccard > 0.5 predicts failure, 5/6 accuracy, ρ=−0.90)\n\nPractical guidelines: (1) verify each method operates at edge-level granularity, (2) compute pairwise Jaccard before investing in multi-method validation (>0.50 → use best single method).\n\n## Related Work Section (from paper §2)\n\nThe paper cites:\n- **Circuit discovery methods**: EAP-IG [Syed et al. 2023], EP [Kramár et al. 2024], ACDC [Conmy et al. 2023], IFR [Zhang & Nanda 2024]\n- **Ensemble approaches**: Feature selection stability [Nogueira & Brown 2016], ensemble diversity [Kuncheva & Whitaker 2003], CIRCUS [Parekh et al. 2026] (within-method threshold diversity), continuous score averaging [Mondorf et al. 2025], PIE [Anonymous 2026] (iterative pruning ensembles)\n- **Evaluation**: CPR/CMD from [Conmy et al. 2023]\n- **Tasks**: IOI circuit [Wang et al. 2023], Factual associations [Meng et al. 2022]\n- **Models**: GPT-2 [Radford et al. 2019], Qwen [Bai et al. 2023]\n\nTotal: 14 references.\n\n## Your Review Focus (Novelty + Related Work)\n\nEvaluate:\n1. **Novelty of contribution**: Is CSS genuinely new or just a formalization of something obvious? Is the \"negative result\" sufficiently insightful? Do the failure mode analyses provide new understanding?\n2. **Positioning relative to prior work**: \n   - Mondorf et al. 2025 (\"Comparing circuit discovery methods\") — how does this paper differ? Is the comparison adequate?\n   - CIRCUS (Parekh et al. 2026) — within-method threshold diversity vs cross-method consensus. Is the distinction clear?\n   - PIE (Anonymous 2026) — pruning ensembles. Overlapping territory?\n3. **Missing related work**: Are there important works not cited? Consider:\n   - Other consensus/ensemble methods in interpretability\n   - Broader feature selection literature\n   - Other circuit evaluation beyond CPR/CMD\n   - Multi-method comparisons in XAI more broadly\n4. **Scope of claims vs evidence**: With n=6 configurations, 2 models, 4 tasks — are the claims appropriately scoped? The \"empirically supported heuristic\" framing for Jaccard diagnostic — sufficient?\n5. **Significance for the community**: Will practitioners actually use these guidelines? Does this change how people do circuit discovery?\n6. **Related work completeness**: Only 14 references for an EMNLP paper — is this enough? Missing important citations?\n\n## Output Format\n\nProvide your review in this structure:\n```\n## R2 Review: Novelty & Related Work\n\n### Summary (2-3 sentences)\n\n### Strengths\n- S1: ...\n- S2: ...\n- S3: ...\n\n### Weaknesses\n- W1: ...\n- W2: ...\n- W3: ...\n\n### Questions for Authors\n- Q1: ...\n- Q2: ...\n\n### Minor Issues\n- ...\n\n### Scores\n- Soundness: X/5\n- Excitement: X/5\n- Overall: X/5\n- Reproducibility: X/5\n- Confidence: X/5\n```\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1473,"cache_read_input_tokens":60070,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1473},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d5948ce3-0bd6-4774-9a29-31d903f57111","uuid":"4b0800ed-7153-4018-a475-b61ce8cf939d"}
